bevy-horizon: a fragment-to-fragment barrier without WAIT_FOR_IDLE (NVK_SWITCH_FRAG_BARRIER)

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 953fa75a, after 0001-0028. scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it; this text before the first
"diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

A pipeline barrier whose sources and destinations are all fragment stages, with color attachment
or sampled access, waits for the whole 3D engine (WAIT_FOR_IDLE). On Maxwell B,
PIXEL_SHADER_BARRIER waits only for earlier pixel shaders, as deko3d's DkBarrier_Fragments does.
NVK_SWITCH_FRAG_BARRIER=1 uses it for color attachment and sampled reads and writes, =2 for
depth/stencil attachments too; 0, the default, keeps WAIT_FOR_IDLE. Barriers from an undefined
layout keep the full wait (ZCULL may be initialized through the copy engine). It logs the first,
1000th and 100000th use.

The change is nebadasSwifty's, from masseffect-nx's NVK patch
(https://github.com/nebadasSwifty/masseffect-nx, mesa/mesa-switch-masseffect.patch;
MIT, as its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md puts its mesa/ changes).

